\section*{Overview}
This repository contains the full scientific documentation suite for the
\textbf{Temporal Symmetry Astrophysics Simulation Engine (TSSE)}.
All documents are written in standard \LaTeX{} using the \texttt{article}
class and rely on AMS mathematical packages for theorem environments,
Hamiltonian formalism, and symplectic analysis.

The documentation includes:
\begin{itemize}
  \item Core white sheet (theoretical foundation)
  \item Temporal Symmetry Reversibility Theorem
  \item Empirical verification logs
  \item Stress-testing matrices
  \item Architectural blueprint descriptions
\end{itemize}

\section*{Directory Structure}
\begin{verbatim}
docs/
 ├── main.tex              % Primary white sheet
 ├── theorem.tex           % Reversibility theorem + proof
 ├── verification.tex      % Empirical validation & logs
 ├── stress-tests.tex      % Adversarial chaos & hardware tests
 ├── macros.tex            % Custom commands & math operators
 └── references.bib        % BibTeX file (optional)
\end{verbatim}

\section*{Required Packages}
The following packages are used throughout the documentation:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \texttt{amsmath}, \texttt{amssymb}, \texttt{amsthm}
  \item \texttt{geometry}
  \item \texttt{hyperref}
  \item \texttt{physics} (optional)
  \item \texttt{mathtools}
\end{itemize}

All packages are standard and available in modern \TeX{} distributions
(\TeX{}Live, MiK\TeX{}, Mac\TeX{}).

\section*{Compilation Instructions}
Compile using \texttt{pdflatex} or \texttt{lualatex}:

\begin{verbatim}
pdflatex main.tex
bibtex main (if using references)
pdflatex main.tex
pdflatex main.tex
\end{verbatim}

Multiple passes ensure theorem numbering, cross-references, and citations
resolve correctly.

\section*{Extending the Documentation}
To add new sections:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item Create a new \texttt{.tex} file in the \texttt{docs/} directory.
  \item Add your content using the existing theorem, lemma, and proof
        environments defined in \texttt{macros.tex}.
  \item Include the file in \texttt{main.tex} using:
\begin{verbatim}
\input{<filename>}
\end{verbatim}
\end{enumerate}

\section*{Math Environments}
The following environments are pre-defined:
\begin{verbatim}
\newtheorem{theorem}{Theorem}
\newtheorem{lemma}{Lemma}
\newtheorem{definition}{Definition}
\end{verbatim}

These support the formal structure of Hamiltonian mechanics, symplectic
geometry, and temporal symmetry proofs.

\section*{Versioning}
All documents should include:
\begin{itemize}
  \item Version number
  \item Date of last modification
  \item Author attribution: C. Matthew Blackwell
\end{itemize}

\section*{Purpose}
This documentation suite provides the formal mathematical foundation,
verification evidence, and architectural description of the TSSE. It is
intended for scientific review, archival, and reproducibility analysis.

